From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:33:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: End the reader's buffer where its data ends after
 moving or growing it.

The reader's buffer holds its text NUL-terminated, and its parsers stop at
the NUL rather than at the count of what was read.  Moving the unread part
to the front left the old text behind it, and pushing an entity's text did
not terminate it, so whatever came after the data was read as if it were
data.  Nothing looked there before, but a check of what follows the root
element does, and found the old text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/saxreader.c b/dlls/msxml3/saxreader.c
index 5e338f07a4d..a8a8e1c754b 100644
--- a/dlls/msxml3/saxreader.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/saxreader.c
@@ -2367,6 +2367,8 @@ static void saxreader_shrink(struct saxlocator *locator)
 
         buffer->written = size;
         buffer->cur = 0;
+        /* what was read stops here as everywhere else, not at what was there before the move */
+        *(WCHAR *)&buffer->data[buffer->written] = 0;
     }
 }
 
@@ -4675,7 +4677,7 @@ static void saxreader_push_entity(struct saxlocator *locator, const struct text_
     if (needed)
     {
         if (!saxreader_array_reserve(locator, (void **)&buffer->data, &buffer->allocated,
-                buffer->written + needed * sizeof(WCHAR), sizeof(*buffer->data)))
+                buffer->written + (needed + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR), sizeof(*buffer->data)))
         {
             return saxreader_set_error(locator, E_OUTOFMEMORY);
         }
@@ -4694,6 +4696,7 @@ static void saxreader_push_entity(struct saxlocator *locator, const struct text_
         memcpy(dst, src, size);
 
         buffer->written += needed * sizeof(WCHAR);
+        *(WCHAR *)&buffer->data[buffer->written] = 0;
     }
 
     entity->visited = true;
